{
  "results": [
    {
      "comments": [
        {
          "commentType": "FUNCTION",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Critical isomerohydrolase in the retinoid cycle involved in regeneration of 11-cis-retinal, the chromophore of rod and cone opsins. Catalyzes the cleavage and isomerization of all-trans-retinyl fatty acid esters to 11-cis-retinol which is further oxidized by 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase to 11-cis-retinal for use as visual chromophore (PubMed:16116091). Essential for the production of 11-cis retinal for both rod and cone photoreceptors (PubMed:17848510). Also capable of catalyzing the isomerization of lutein to meso-zeaxanthin an eye-specific carotenoid (PubMed:28874556). The soluble form binds vitamin A (all-trans-retinol), making it available for LRAT processing to all-trans-retinyl ester. The membrane form, palmitoylated by LRAT, binds all-trans-retinyl esters, making them available for IMH (isomerohydrolase) processing to all-cis-retinol. The soluble form is regenerated by transferring its palmitoyl groups onto 11-cis-retinol, a reaction catalyzed by LRAT (By similarity)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
          "reaction": {
            "ecNumber": "3.1.1.64",
            "name": "an all-trans-retinyl ester + H2O = 11-cis-retinol + a fatty acid + H(+)"
          }
        },
        {
          "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
          "reaction": {
            "ecNumber": "5.3.3.22",
            "name": "lutein = (3R,3'S)-zeaxanthin"
          }
        },
        {
          "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
          "reaction": {
            "ecNumber": "3.1.1.64",
            "name": "all-trans-retinyl hexadecanoate + H2O = 11-cis-retinol + hexadecanoate + H(+)"
          }
        },
        {
          "commentType": "COFACTOR"
        },
        {
          "commentType": "BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES"
        },
        {
          "commentType": "SUBUNIT",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Interacts with MYO7A; this mediates light-dependent intracellular transport of RPE65"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "INTERACTION"
        },
        {
          "commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION",
          "subcellularLocations": [
            {
              "location": {
                "value": "Cytoplasm"
              }
            },
            {
              "location": {
                "value": "Cell membrane"
              }
            },
            {
              "location": {
                "value": "Microsome membrane"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "TISSUE SPECIFICITY",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Retina (at protein level). Retinal pigment epithelium specific"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "PTM",
          "texts": [
            {
              "value": "Palmitoylation by LRAT regulates ligand binding specificity; the palmitoylated form (membrane form) specifically binds all-trans-retinyl-palmitate, while the soluble unpalmitoylated form binds all-trans-retinol (vitamin A) (By similarity)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "commentType": "DISEASE",
          "disease": {
